## 14. Final project acceptance gate

The overall enhancement effort is ready for owner acceptance only when all applicable conditions are met:

- All governing capability claims are audited with evidence or explicitly marked unverified/missing-source.
- Contradictions, overlaps, rejected/deferred items and owner decisions are traceable.
- Architecture diagrams and descriptions accurately distinguish verified-current and proposed-target elements.
- Roadmap increments are completed only against measurable acceptance criteria, with validation evidence and documented remaining work.
- Data sources and licenses have approved status for each shipped use; unknown rights block shipping that use.
- Security, privacy, authorization, tenant isolation, prompt-injection, secret handling and retention controls are tested for changed surfaces.
- Quantitative/financial claims have reproducible methodology, appropriate out-of-sample validation, costs/limitations and approved wording; unvalidated claims are not shown as fact.
- New AI behavior has versioning, evidence/citation checks, bounded tools, monitoring, abstention, and human review/change governance.
- Simulated activity is isolated and labeled; no autonomous/live order execution exists without separate explicit approval.
- Observability, alerts, runbooks, feature exposure, migration/recovery and rollback are ready for affected paths.
- Documentation, user-facing states, accessibility and release notes are current.
- Test and baseline limitations are reported accurately; no failures were hidden or tests weakened.
- No unapproved dependency, external service, cost, production action, destructive change, or unauthorized disclosure occurred.

Conclude with an evidence-based status: **accepted for owner review**, **ready for a named release gate**, or **blocked with specific decisions/evidence needed**. Do not label the whole application “production ready” unless an authorized release review has established that scope.

